 "brief": "A part-cooling duct in PLA (FDM, layers along Z) for a 3D printer. A 40 x 40 x 10 mm fan (22 g) bolts flat onto its top face (the plane z = 40) with two M3 screws on a diagonal (x, y = -16, -16 and 16, 16) that thread 6 mm into the duct. Air goes down from a 36 mm round inlet under the fan and narrows to a 30 x 6 mm slot outlet at z = 0 (x = -15 to 15, y = 10 to 16). The duct hangs from the carriage by two M3 screws through a tab on the back: the tab is the plane y = -20, screws at x = -12 and 12, z = 30. Keep it inside x = -20 to 20, y = -20 to 20, z = 0 to 40. The carriage shakes it at up to 3 g in any direction. Walls 1.2 mm. Safety factor 2.",
